## Discrepancies, Ambiguity, and Annotator Differences 

One example where the manual and automated methods differ is Franklin Street in New York. New York is where the journey begins, yet Franklin Street appears in section 6 of the novel, towards the end of the journey. This raises questions about whether the car actually passed through this location or whether it was simply mentioned by the machine in its generated text. Another interesting detail is that there are multiple streets named Franklin Street in New York, and the automated method identifies several of them. However, this does not necessarily mean that the car travelled through all these streets. It makes us question whether the system is identifying actual locations the car encountered or simply matching place named mentioned in the text to multiple possible geographical locations. 


