Manual annotation also has inconsistencies. For example, Columbia appears five times as separate points in the manual annotations. This may have resulted from an annotator selecting yes to all in Recogito without checking whether they represented distinct locations. As well as it seems that two different annotators annotated Columbia once twice and the other three times. Additionally, the selected Columbia appears to be in Tennessee, despite being relatively far from the expected highway route. This illustrates that human annotation is not automatically accurate either. Different annotators can make different decisions, and mistakes during annotation can create misleading spatial concentrations.


